{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhooW2AajsZhnCEZpNz6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate and it passes the self-check. The check prints `OK`, and its short trial fit gave a finite ELPD-LOO of −1026.3. That number is from a 100-draw, single-chain smoke run, so it isn't comparable to the fully fitted models' scores.\n\n- **Model:** `global_local_balance_representativeness`\n- **Which model I refined:** `iter0_candidate3`, the strongest model on the menu. It is statistically tied with the incumbent (1.4 ± 12.2 nats behind). It scores a sequence on heads/tails balance plus irregularity, and each person has their own decision sensitivity.\n- **The one change:** it previously averaged overall balance and short-window balance (windows of 2–4 flips) with equal fixed weights. Now a fitted parameter, `global_share`, decides how much of the balance judgment rests on the whole sequence's heads/tails balance and how much on the short windows. Everything else is unchanged.\n- **Why:** this targets the critique finding that survived the multiple-testing correction. Among pairs with similar switch counts, people chose the more balanced sequence 72% of the time, against 64% predicted by the incumbent. If the model is right, the fit should put more weight on overall balance.\n\nWhat isn't verified yet:\n- **Convergence:** a single chain can't report R-hat. Convergence and the 30-minute speed limit are only tested in admission's full fit.\n- **LOO reliability:** the smoke fit flagged 9.1% of trials with a high Pareto k, well over the 1% tolerance. That may only reflect how short the trial fit was, but I haven't confirmed it.\n- **Novelty:** the novelty check against the live models doesn't run here. The predictions could come out too close to `iter0_candidate3` if the fitted balance weighting ends up near the old equal split.\n\nThe files are in `.../experiment1/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_5/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3520,"cache_read_input_tokens":64242,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3520,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c22b9c68-3b2a-4c06-9485-e0689228fe06","uuid":"2b35f0bb-7db7-4083-b40b-de439df44d0e","timestamp":"2026-10-04T20:13:04.554Z","request_id":"req_011CfhooV6N2X4BwG2gsUjDS"}
